A||N||7||fierovette||Another problem, it never ends!||||5||
Z||000000||fierovette||10-06-2001||08:19 AM||||Battery light went on last night, guage reading about 11 volts & slowly droping. The belt is tight. Alternator?? Regulator?? Bad Battery?? Whats an easy test to determine what to replace?||||reg||5
Z||000001||johnt671||10-06-2001||09:36 AM||||When mine did that it turned out to be the alt.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Banzai||10-06-2001||09:40 AM||||Make sure all connections are clean and tight. Otherwise, it's probobly the alternator. You can replace it($80-100) or rebuild it yourself($20-30).<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||10-06-2001||09:54 AM||||I would also be it's the alternator. Because of the high engine compartment temp's on the Fieros, belts and electronics tend to suffer. I replaced my alternator in about 2 hours but everything came apart pretty easy. Good luck!||||reg||9
Z||000004||Fformula88||10-06-2001||11:47 AM||||My vote is also alternator.  Just a word of warning about the rebuilt ones... they often go bad very quickly too!  It seems whenever the factory alternator goes in a car and isn't replaced with a new one, people are always replacing them again and again.  Its your best bet with those symptoms.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||10-06-2001||01:38 PM||||Check the Red HOT wire that attaches to the back of the Alt. They sometimes corrode and break apart and remain inside the boot.||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||06:00 PM||||My car had the same symptoms. <BR>It was the alternator.<P>Got a higher amp rebuilt (with guarantee) one from NAPA.<P>Quick easy change.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||roadwarrior||10-06-2001||09:47 PM||||sounds like a bad alt to me, try putting a volmeter right on the alternator.<P>||||reg||1
